yes(413,'D','A carboxylic acid reacts with sodium hydrogencarbonate to release carbon dioxide bubbles: RCOOH + NaHCO₃ → RCOONa + H₂O + CO₂. This effervescence identifies the carboxyl group among the choices.',[CARB,'https://edupadi.com/classroom/lessons/jamb/chemistry/1992/page/5'],question='The functional group present in an organic compound which gives bubbles on treatment with a saturated solution of NaHCO₃ is the',options=['Hydroxyl group','Carboalkoxyl group','Carbonyl group','Carboxyl group'],audit='Missing effervescence observation recovered from matching EduPadi1992 question, not inferred solely from answer.',check='bicarbonate-balance')
