yes(419,'C','Both uranium atoms have atomic number 92, so each has 92 protons. Their mass numbers differ: 235 − 92 = 143 neutrons and 238 − 92 = 146 neutrons. Atoms of the same element with different neutron numbers are isotopes.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/2-3-atomic-structure-and-symbolism'],question='Two atoms represented as ²³⁵₉₂U and ²³⁸₉₂U are',check='isotope-count')
